  "body": "```py\r\nIn [58]: a = torch.randn(()).requires_grad_()\r\n\r\nIn [59]: b = torch.tensor(False)\r\n\r\nIn [60]: c = torch.ones(())\r\n\r\nIn [61]: torch.where(b, a/0, c)\r\nOut[61]: tensor(1., grad_fn=<SWhereBackward>)\r\n\r\nIn [62]: torch.autograd.grad(torch.where(b, a/0, c), a)\r\nOut[62]: (tensor(nan),)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is yet another case of weird behavior because we don't differentiate \"no gradient\" vs. \"zero gradient\". The not-used branch computes gradient 0/0 and that becomes NaN... \r\n\r\nThis makes writing NaN avoiding ops kinda difficult without doing a custom autograd Function. \r\n\n\ncc @ezyang @albanD @zou3519 @gqchen @pearu @nikitaved @soulitzer @Lezcano @Varal7",
